  "authored_scope": "Supported:\n- Panel size 2..6.\n- 2..6 panels per axis when sampled, with independent row and column counts, fitting within 30x30.\n- A random two-colour motif from the colours excluding 0 and 5, with a strict majority and 1..(s^2-1)//2 minority cells.\n- A random set of solid panels: at least one, at most half.\n- Random-walk noise blobs of 5 that may cross dividers and cover both kinds of panel.\n- Explicit latent arguments that reconstruct all five fixtures.\n\nPanel sizes 5..6, layouts of 5 or more panels per axis, and non-square layouts are synthetic extensions beyond the fixtures.\n\nNot supported:\n- Unequal panel sizes.\n- Thicker dividers.\n- Motifs with three or more colours.\n- Tied colour counts.\n- Noise in colours other than 5.\n- Scenes where no clean pattern panel exists.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Grid dimensions are rows*(size+1)-1 by cols*(size+1)-1, at most 30 per side.",
    "The motif uses exactly two colours, neither 0 nor 5, and its majority is strict.",
    "There is at least one solid panel and at least one pattern panel; random sampling uses at most half the panels as solids.",
    "Every divider row and column keeps at least one visible 0.",
    "No panel row or column has all its panel cells covered by 5, so the divider detector cannot be fooled.",
    "At least one pattern panel is noise-free, so the motif is the unique clean non-uniform panel.",
    "Every solid panel has at least one visible cell at a motif-majority position, so it cannot be mistaken for a pattern panel.",
    "Every sample is non-identity, because pattern panels lose their minority cells in the output.",
    "Explicit noise maps are checked by the same constraints and raise ValueError if they give an ambiguous scene."
  ],
